        "orario": "05:03",
        "timestamp": 1780369402,
        "contenuto_esteso": "Live Middle East war live: Israeli military intercepts projectiles from Lebanon Middle East Issued on: 02/06/2026 - 05:03 Modified: 02/06/2026 - 08:41 Tensions along the Israel-Lebanon border continued early on Tuesday as Israeli air defences intercepted incoming projectiles, despite US President Donald Trump’s claim that he had brokered an end to fighting between Israel and Hezbollah. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates. 02/06/2026 - 08:39 Iran has not yet sent its response to US in talks, Mehr says ⁠Iran has ​not yet responded ​to a proposed final agreement with the United ​States ‌aimed at ending ⁠the conflict between the ‌two countries, and discussions on ⁠the final text are continuing in ​Tehran, a source ‌close to the Iranian negotiating team told ‌Mehr News on Tuesday. The ​source said Iran was reviewing the proposal cautiously because ​of what it ​sees as ​a history of US non-compliance ​and longstanding mistrust. \"Based on previous experiences, Iran is seeking tangible and real ⁠benefits,\" the source said. 02/06/2026 - 08:36 'Nothing can justify' prolonged Israeli occupation in Lebanon, says French FM France's foreign minister has said that nothing could justify Israeli troops remaining deep inside Lebanon, after Israel and Hezbollah clashed overnight despite a US announcement that both sides had agreed to halt fighting. \"Nothing can justify the continuation of military operations and Israel's prolonged occupation deep inside Lebanese territory,\" Jean-Noël Barrot told France TV. 02/06/2026 - 08:17 Clashes with Israel continue in southern Lebanon despite Trump promise of de-escalation Israel and Hezbollah clashed overnight despite US President Donald Trump's announcement that both sides had agreed to halt fighting ahead of US-hosted talks between Israel and Lebanon on Tuesday. The overnight clashes came after Lebanon said Iran-backed Hezbollah had accepted a US proposal for a \"mutual cessation of attacks\" after Trump said he persuaded the warring sides to de-escalate. But Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu appeared to cast doubt on any truce, and a report by US news outlet Axios on Monday said Trump called him \"fucking crazy\" and accused him of putting Iran peace talks at risk. FRANCE 24's Renée Davis reports from Beirut. 02/06/2026 - 08:14 Trump clashes with Netanyahu over Israel's Lebanon offensive, US media reports US President Donald Trump laid in to Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu during an expletive-filled phone call to discuss US fears that Israel's continued offensive in Lebanon and is jeopardising hopes of a peace deal with Iran, media outlet Axios reported. FRANCE 24's correspondent Fraser Jackson gives the details from Washington. 02/06/2026 - 07:38 Israel, Lebanon set for new round of talks in Washington A new round of talks between representatives from Lebanon and Israel is due to take place on Tuesday and Wednesday in Washington. Lebanese President Joseph Aoun on Monday issued a statement reiterating Beirut's commitment to negotiations, saying they are “safer than war\". 02/06/2026 - 05:01 Israeli military intercepts projectiles from Lebanon Israeli air defences intercepted projectiles launched from Lebanon into northern Israel early on Tuesday, just hours after US President Donald Trump announced that fighting would end. The Israeli military said early Tuesday air defences intercepted two projectiles from Lebanon, hours after US President Donald Trump announced that fighting would end. “Following the sirens that sounded at 01:35 (2235 GMT) in several areas in northern Israel, the IAF intercepted two projectiles that crossed from Lebanon into Israeli territory,” the military said on Telegram. A “suspicious aerial target” that later fell in Israeli territory near the Lebanese border was also identified, it said, adding that no injuries were reported. 02/06/2026 - 05:01 Welcome to the FRANCE 24 liveblog covering events in the Middle East. You can catch up on what happened yesterday here . Yesterday's key developments: • US President Donald Trump on Monday said he had persuaded Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu not to send troops into southern Beirut . • The Lebanese presidential office posted a statement by Lebanon's embassy in Washington saying Hezbollah had accepted a US proposal calling for a \"reciprocal cessation of attacks\". • Hezbollah claimed several attacks late Monday on Israeli targets in south Lebanon , hours after Trump said the Iran -backed group had agreed that \"all shooting will stop\". (FRANCE 24 with Reuters, AP and AFP)"
